          "type": "tool_call_delta",
          "declarationKey": "note-r1-decl-1",
          "argumentsDelta": "{\"path\":\"Research/Ring facts the scenes must respect.md\",\"content\":\"---\\ntype: synthesis\\nsources:\\n  - \\\"[[Rings of Saturn]]\\\"\\n  - \\\"[[Asteroid belt]]\\\"\\n---\\n\\n# Ring facts the scenes must respect\\n\\n- The station sits in the Keeler Gap at the outer edge of the A ring, where Daphnis orbits and keeps the gap open.\\n- The ring is a sheet, not a cloud: 10 m thick where the station works, up to 1 km elsewhere. From fifty metres up it is a floor.\\n- 99.9% water ice, particles from dust to 10 m. There is nothing to harvest but water.\\n- The Cassini Division is 4,800 km of near-empty space between the B and A rings, kept clear by Mimas. A place to lose a ship.\\n- Spokes in the B ring turn with the planet, not with the ring. Let a character see one and not explain it.\\n- Ring rain: 4,800 to 44,000 kg/s falling into Saturn. The rings could be gone in 300 million years. Nobody on the station will see it, and everyone knows.\\n\"}"
